00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:02.000
Nothing! I would have known!

00:47:02.590 --> 00:47:05.280
You're a better scientist than that. Think about it.

00:47:07.010 --> 00:47:10.510
Where did that statistically insignificant protomatter come from?

00:47:12.360 --> 00:47:15.340
Okay, that's a good question.

00:47:16.420 --> 00:47:18.380
Yeah, I thought so.

00:47:28.740 --> 00:47:29.800
You've had crewmates die.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:32.130
Does it ever stop hurting?

00:47:34.790 --> 00:47:37.570
No, just learn to live with it.

00:47:38.410 --> 00:47:39.690
That's a terrible way to live.

00:47:40.750 --> 00:47:42.260
Yes, it is.

00:47:42.400 --> 00:47:45.370
But it's better than the alternative.

00:47:51.300 --> 00:47:51.680
Kirk here.

00:47:53.600 --> 00:47:56.080
Found something coising about the alien vessel.

00:47:56.880 --> 00:47:58.460
I'm on my way. Kirk out.

00:48:00.890 --> 00:48:01.550
Hold that thought.

00:48:14.680 --> 00:48:15.960
Tell me you have something for me.

00:48:16.720 --> 00:48:20.820
Instant Soulguard and I have completed a full sensor sweep of the alien vessel.

00:48:21.780 --> 00:48:27.630
The ship's technology is on par with the Federation's, but we did detect one anomaly.

00:48:28.580 --> 00:48:29.960
I found residual traces of the alien vessel.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:32.000
of protomatter in the vessel's cargo hold?

00:48:32.520 --> 00:48:33.140
Of course.

00:48:35.110 --> 00:48:38.130
Sabotage is not a logical possibility.

00:48:38.150 --> 00:48:42.670
It is not profitable to kill your trading partners.

00:48:43.800 --> 00:48:46.760
On the other hand, if you don't trust your trading partners,

00:48:47.370 --> 00:48:49.630
you might not give them the part of the manual that says,

00:48:49.960 --> 00:48:51.280
don't blow yourself up.

00:48:52.500 --> 00:48:54.180
We know from Mr. Scott's report

00:48:54.180 --> 00:48:56.840
that the terraforming team was behind schedule,

00:48:57.450 --> 00:48:59.910
a business transaction to enhance their transport.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.700
order matrices would seem logical.

00:49:05.140 --> 00:49:06.240
What did they trade for?

00:49:10.900 --> 00:49:12.690
Uhura, hail the alien vessel.

00:49:13.730 --> 00:49:15.070
Call Dr. Marcus to the bridge.

00:49:16.150 --> 00:49:18.850
Alien vessel, this is Captain James T. Kirk.

00:49:19.470 --> 00:49:20.590
Yes, Captain.

00:49:21.610 --> 00:49:23.960
Traded total matter technology

00:49:23.960 --> 00:49:25.990
to the Lapa-3 outpost.

00:49:27.230 --> 00:49:28.170
What did you trade for?

00:49:29.370 --> 00:49:29.970
We don't.

00:49:30.350 --> 00:49:33.550
Highlight confidentiality of our trade partners.

00:49:33.890 --> 00:49:34.710
Even after they're dead?

00:49:35.500 --> 00:49:38.480
That's regrettable, but yes.

00:49:41.110 --> 00:49:43.850
If you would like to arrange a trade zone,

00:49:45.540 --> 00:49:48.300
we think you will find it as profitable as we would.

00:49:48.460 --> 00:49:52.890
The price of continued negotiations is information.

00:50:00.220 --> 00:50:01.620
You're going to negotiate with them?

00:50:02.760 --> 00:50:05.770
No, I'm going to play poker with them.

00:50:08.780 --> 00:50:15.430
...a set of transporter matrices and head for proto-matter creation.

00:50:16.780 --> 00:50:18.000
Who did you deliver them to?

00:50:18.570 --> 00:50:20.550
Robert DeWitt, the trade officer.

00:50:21.680 --> 00:50:24.460
Dr. Robert DeWitt, the assistant project director.

00:50:25.210 --> 00:50:28.560
DeWitt? Trade officer? He was never...

00:50:30.640 --> 00:50:33.890
Oh my god, he must have been desperate.

00:50:37.040 --> 00:50:39.960
He was as passionate about terraforming Lappa III as I was.

00:50:40.790 --> 00:50:44.750
The more the project fell behind, the more distraught he became.

00:50:45.320 --> 00:50:48.160
He must have convinced himself the risk was worth it.

00:50:48.280 --> 00:50:56.720
Thank you, Ferengi Trader.

00:50:58.840 --> 00:50:59.560
Yes, I do.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:12.880
that govern my people captain one peace is good for business two war it's even better for business

00:51:13.980 --> 00:51:17.180
either way we're open for business

00:51:31.920 --> 00:51:36.520
L, set course for Starbase 26, Warp Factor 4.

00:51:53.500 --> 00:51:57.560
Marie, I yelled at you. Thank you for finding out the truth.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:14.960
wanted. Does it help? A little, but I feel so empty. I thought my work, my friends. I can't know how you

00:52:14.960 --> 00:52:27.960
feel. If it were the Enterprise, I think I'd feel the same. And it will never go away. You said so

00:52:27.960 --> 00:52:29.830
yourself. No, I'll be okay.

